From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: UebelAndre <github@uebelandre.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 12:05:26 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(lexer): follow the spec for comment lines, `\x` escapes
 and raw byte strings

Three places where the lexer diverged from the Starlark spec, each
surfacing as an error on valid code:

Comment-only lines took part in indentation, so a comment indented
deeper than its block, or less, produced INDENT or DEDENT tokens and the
parser reported "Unexpected indentation". Blank and comment-only lines
are now skipped for indentation, as the spec says.

`\xHH` consumed up to six hexadecimal digits, so `"\x41A"` was rejected
as a value too large instead of being `"AA"`. The escape takes exactly
two digits; fewer is an error.

Raw byte strings (`rb"\d"`, `br'\d'`) were unescaped as if they were
not raw and reported invalid escapes. They now get the raw treatment
text strings already had: a backslash only escapes the quote.
---
 crates/starpls_lexer/src/lib.rs            | 11 ++--
 crates/starpls_lexer/src/tests.rs          | 48 +++++++++++++++++
 crates/starpls_lexer/src/unescape.rs       | 44 ++++++++++-----
 crates/starpls_lexer/src/unescape/tests.rs | 62 +++++++++++++++++++++-
 crates/starpls_parser/src/text.rs          |  2 +-
 5 files changed, 149 insertions(+), 18 deletions(-)

diff --git a/crates/starpls_lexer/src/lib.rs b/crates/starpls_lexer/src/lib.rs
index 90d3a48..fbe2a43 100644
--- a/crates/starpls_lexer/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/starpls_lexer/src/lib.rs
@@ -330,9 +330,14 @@ impl Cursor<'_> {
 
                     let last_indent = self.indents.last().cloned().unwrap_or(0);
 
-                    // If we are at an equal indentation level, or are currently at a newline or EOF, we can just
-                    // emit the whitespace that we consumed.
-                    if indent == last_indent || self.first() == '\n' || self.is_eof() {
+                    // If we are at an equal indentation level, or are currently at a newline, a
+                    // comment or EOF, we can just emit the whitespace that we consumed: blank and
+                    // comment-only lines do not take part in indentation.
+                    if indent == last_indent
+                        || self.first() == '\n'
+                        || self.first() == '#'
+                        || self.is_eof()
+                    {
                         self.state = CursorState::AfterLeadingSpaces;
                         let pos_within_token = self.reset_pos_within_token();
                         if pos_within_token == 0 {
diff --git a/crates/starpls_lexer/src/tests.rs b/crates/starpls_lexer/src/tests.rs
index 421ed4b..639ac56 100644
--- a/crates/starpls_lexer/src/tests.rs
+++ b/crates/starpls_lexer/src/tests.rs
@@ -945,3 +945,51 @@ fn test_crlf_unterminated_string() {
